Add the experimental, default-off `--extended-newtype-bases` option, requiring
`--general-newtypes` and `--type-system-refresh`. It permits ORDINAL, datatype
(including tuple and codatatype), and all three arrow families as newtype bases.
Newtypes retain nominal typing and checked constraints; visible base operations
keep their instantiated signatures. Nominal updates recheck their predicates,
and exact datatype identity casts preserve statement evaluation order and
nominal conversion metadata without added closure layers. Existing base
restrictions remain when the option is disabled.
